<h2>6. Concurrency &amp; Load Verification Benchmark</h2>
<p>
The system was benchmarked under an automated high-contention test script simulating 500 concurrent checkout attempts targeting 1 solitary unit of stock:
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Test Metric</th>
      <th>Observed Benchmark Value</th>
      <th>Evaluation Assessment</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Total Simultaneous Requests</td>
      <td>500 HTTP POST Requests</td>
      <td>Stress load simulated</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Successful Dispatches</td>
      <td>Exactly 1 Committed (HTTP 200)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-success">PASSED</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Rejected Requests</td>
      <td>499 Conflict Responses (HTTP 409)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-success">PASSED</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Negative Stock Incidents</td>
      <td>0 (Zero)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-success">100% ACID Integrity</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Average Response Latency</td>
      <td>28ms</td>
      <td>Sub-50ms SLA maintained</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

